      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "intro",
      "text": "The aspose.page module provides entry points for working with PostScript, EPS, XPS, and PDF content, with dedicated submodules for each format. The aspose.page.ps submodule supports reading and writing PostScript and EPS files, the aspose.page.xps submodule handles XPS documents, the aspose.page.pdf submodule serializes render models to PDF, the aspose.page.image submodule renders documents to raster images, and the aspose.page.mcp submodule offers high-level conversion and metadata extraction tools."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.page",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.image",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.mcp",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.pdf",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.ps",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.xps"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:aspose.page",
      "text": "The aspose.page module serves as the top-level namespace for the Aspose.Page FOSS for Python library, exposing submodules for PostScript, EPS, XPS, PDF, and image processing operations."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
